{
  "goal": "Record a MEMBER INQUIRY capability against MERIDIAN CORE that searches by LAST NAME. (1) Sign on. (2) Open Member Inquiry / Selection. (3) In 'Search by' call choose with option = the searchBy parameter value verbatim (it is the option's underlying value: 'name' or 'number'). (4) Type the query parameter into the Value field. (5) Click Search. (6) A results table appears - use read_table ONCE to capture it into an output named 'matches', requesting exactly these columns: Member No., Name, Shares. (7) Then probe one exceptional state: begin_probe MEMBER_NOT_FOUND, search again for a last name that does not exist such as Zzzznomatch, and declare_outcome MEMBER_NOT_FOUND with a marker you can literally see. (8) declare_done with capability_id 'member.inquire'.",
